2. Signal libsignal — crate `libsignal-keytrans` (Key Transparency verifier)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream:      https://github.com/signalapp/libsignal
Pinned commit: e8cc2dddd578859b4a029c9c94670b24ce2b616a  (2026-09-22)
License:       AGPL-3.0-only (upstream `LICENSE`; crate declares `license.workspace = true`, workspace license = AGPL-3.0-only)

How NYX uses it (unmodified):
  * `vendor/signal/libsignal-keytrans/` — the pinned `rust/keytrans` crate, copied
    as-is. Its `Cargo.toml` is **materialized** during vendoring: every
    `workspace = true` inheritance is rewritten to an explicit version, because the
    crate stands alone here (`scripts/vendor-signal.sh`, guarded by
    `scripts/check-vendor.sh`).
  * `packages/keytrans-wasm/` — thin wrapper (`src/lib.rs`) compiled to
    `wasm32-unknown-unknown` (raw module, no `wasm-bindgen`). `build.sh` generates
    `Cargo.toml` (not committed) with
    `libsignal-keytrans = { path = "<repo>/vendor/signal/libsignal-keytrans" }`;
    `KEYTRANS_PATH` (or the legacy alias `LIBSIGNAL_PATH`) can point at a full
    libsignal checkout while chasing a new pin.
  * Committed build artifact: `packages/keytrans-wasm/dist/keytrans.wasm` (299,924 bytes,
    rebuilt from the vendored source).
  * Client use: `web/src/lib/keyTransparency.ts` (ops `verify_search`,
    `verify_monitor`, `verify_distinguished`, `monitor_next`, `condense_update`)
    wired into the prekey-bundle trust decision by `ktBundleProof.ts`,
    `ktSubject.ts`, `ktMonitoring.ts`, `peerIdentityTrust.ts`. Design/spec: `docs/34`.

Other parts of libsignal were read only as an implementation reference, without
copying code — e.g. the group sender-key design (`docs/16`). The
cross-implementation ratchet checks that DO exist (`docs/30` WS-G(6), `docs/11`
§11.4) are built from a **separate, non-libsodium oracle** (`tools/dr-oracle/`,
Go: `golang.org/x/crypto`, `github.com/cloudflare/circl`) covering X3DH, the KEM,
the keyed-BLAKE2b chain and AEAD in both directions; no libsignal code is built
or shipped for them. A libsignal-based oracle over the full sender-key chain is
still **not implemented**.

